                      Emu68DeviceTree 1.0.0-rc1
                      =========================

                  Display the PiStorm/Emu68 Device Tree
                    Written by Philippe CARPENTIER


WHAT IT IS
==========

Emu68DeviceTree is a MUI browser for the Device Tree published by Emu68
on PiStorm boards. That tool may help the lowlevel PiStorm/Emu68 developers.


REQUIREMENTS
============

  - AmigaOS 3.0 or better. Nothing newer than V36 is called.

  - A machine exposing the devicetree.resource.
    In practice a PiStorm board running Emu68.

  - MUI 3.8 or better.
    http://aminet.net/package/util/libs/mui38usr

  - MCC_NList, MCC_NListview, MCC_NListtree.
    http://aminet.net/package/dev/mui/MCC_NList-0.128
    
  - MCC_HexEdit, by Miloslaw Smyk.
    http://aminet.net/package/dev/mui/MCC_HexEdit


INSTALLATION
============

Copy Emu68DeviceTree wherever you like. The program needs no assign, no
configuration file and no argument. Its settings are the MUI ones, reachable
from the Project menu.


NOTES
=====

